<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Futures setback slows movement.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Futures setback slows movement.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were mixed Friday, with the recent sharp setback in KCBT futures bringing farmer sales to a virtual halt, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>Demand from both the export and domestic side was also generally subdued although a modest pickup in buying interest from some Kansas mills was noted.</p>
<p>They said cool, wet weather may be helping the crop as it attempts to recover from freeze damage. &quot;Rain and cooler temperatures are about as ideal as it can get for wheat trying to regenerate itself after the freeze,&quot; one dealer said.  </p>
